From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:44:05 +0200
Subject: media: cedrus: add MPEG-4 Part 2, H.263 and Sorenson
 Spark decoding support

The MPEG engine of the Allwinner video engine decodes MPEG-4 Part 2
(Simple and Advanced Simple profiles: B-VOPs, quarter sample motion
compensation, interlaced coding, global motion compensation with up to
three warping points, quantisation matrices), H.263 and Sorenson Spark,
whose picture headers it is configured with by the stateless controls.

It does not parse video packet, GOB or slice headers: it decodes a given
number of macroblocks from a given bit position, with a given quantiser,
and stops. The driver programs one hardware run per segment of the
picture which starts with a header, from the slice parameter controls,
which it therefore requires unless the VOL disables the resync markers.

Each capture buffer gets a buffer for the macroblock information and the
not coded flags the engine writes while decoding a P-VOP, and reads back
when it decodes the B-VOPs which use that picture as backward reference
for their direct mode. They are allocated with the first picture decoded
to the buffer and kept until the buffer is freed.

The global motion compensation registers take the affine transform of
ISO/IEC 14496-2 rather than the trajectories of the warping points; the
driver derives it, in the reduced form the engine expects. A warp is
programmed as a translation only when it is one.

Of the MPEG-4 encoder deviations, the engine reproduces the edge
extension from the exact picture size, the two chroma vector derivations
of the DivX quarter sample motion compensation, the DivX chroma field
vector derivation (which the vendor library uses for every bitstream,
although it does not match the standard) and the DivX 5.00 global motion
compensation, which the quirks control advertises.

Only the H.263 modes which the engine supports are accepted: the
version 1 unrestricted motion vectors, the slice structured mode with
ordered, non-rectangular slices and the extended picture type with
custom picture sizes and the rounding type. The engine mis-decodes inter
macroblocks of P pictures in the advanced intra coding mode, which is
therefore rejected along with the modified quantisation mode it comes
with in practice.

Tested on H616 against the ISO/IEC 14496-5 reference decoder with the
ISO/IEC 14496-4 conformance bitstreams of the Simple and Advanced Simple
profiles, the ITU-T H.263 test bitstreams and real world DivX, Xvid,
H.263 and Sorenson Spark files. The output is within the IDCT accuracy
of the reference, with two engine limitations: field motion vectors
whose vertical component exceeds half of the f_code range are wrapped as
if they were in frame units, which shows in about 1% of the field
predicted macroblocks of the 1080i conformance bitstream, and the chroma
prediction of B-VOP direct mode macroblocks differs from the reference
in some bitstreams, luma being exact, as does the chroma prediction of
some quarter sample field motion vectors, for which the engine has no
derivation of the standard; the driver uses the derivation of the vendor
library.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
